{"product_id":"nothing","title":"Nothing","description":"\u003cp\u003e課ﾏRemarkable.課揄ﾛﾓNew York Times Book ReviewFrom Annie Barrows, the acclaimed #1 New York Times課ﾒbestselling coauthor of The Guernsey Literary and Potato Peel Pie Society and the author of the award-winning and bestselling Ivy + Bean books, this teen debut tells the story of Charlotte and Frankie, two high school students and best friends who don課ｪt have magical powers, fight aliens, crash their cars, get pierced, or discover they are royal. They just go to school. And live at home. With their parents. A great read for fans of Becky Albertalli, Louise Rennison, and Adi Alsaid.Nothing ever happens to Charlotte and Frankie. Their lives are nothing like the lives of the girls they read about in their YA novels. They don課ｪt have flowing red hair, and hot romantic encounters never happen課ﾓlet alone meeting a true soul mate. They just go to high school and live at home with their parents, who are pretty normal, all things considered.But when Charlotte decides to write down everything that happens during their sophomore year課ﾓto prove that nothing happens and there is no plot or character development in real life課ﾓshe課ｪs surprised to find that being fifteen isn課ｪt as boring as she thought. It課ｪs weird, heartbreaking, silly, and complicated. And maybe, just perfect.\u003cbr\u003e\nDimensions: 140 x 210\u003cbr\u003e\nAuthor: Barrows Annie\u003cbr\u003e\nISBN: 9780062668233\u003cbr\u003e\nFormat: Hardcover\u003cbr\u003e\nPages: 224\u003c\/p\u003e","brand":"bookhero.ae","offers":[{"title":"Default Title","offer_id":45262382301337,"sku":"16RB-1-9780062668233","price":20.0,"currency_code":"AED","in_stock":true}],"thumbnail_url":"\/\/cdn.shopify.com\/s\/files\/1\/0580\/5696\/6297\/files\/67e7ecaebf665_Nothing_20Barrows_20Annie.jpg?v=1752084534","url":"https:\/\/bookhero.ae\/products\/nothing","provider":"Dubai - Buy Used\/Second-Hand Books - Book Loop Book","version":"1.0","type":"link"}